# Repos to "catch up" instead of pull.
#
# List a machine-env repo NAME here (one per line, same names as in a
# *.machine-env-repos manifest, or an auto-discovered $HOME/Yew/*-setup repo) to
# switch it into catch-up mode. Comments (#) and blank lines are ignored.
#
# In catch-up mode gar measures how far the CURRENT branch is behind its own git
# upstream (@{u}) and offers to run `git fetch` + `git rebase @{u}` on whatever
# branch is checked out (a clean working tree is still required). This suits
# repos where you sit on a feature branch and want it caught up to mainline,
# rather than pulling the configured branch from origin.
#
# A catch-up repo whose current branch has no upstream is flagged (WARN) rather
# than silently skipped. Catch-up findings are advisory (WARN) — they never fail
# the run.
#
# Machine-local overlays live in ~/.config/gar/d/ and can add platform- or
# role-scoped catch-up lists (e.g. mac.machine-env-catchup).
#
# Example:
# my-feature-repo
